    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d797">

                <pb facs="0698" n="688" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg688"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">124.93/5–1249: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister-Counselor of Embassy in China</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Clark</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Canton</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-05-12T16:00:00+08:00">May 12, 1949—4 p.
                            m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 13—6:09 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Cantel 368. Reliable sources inform us Liu Po-cheng<anchor n="44"
                        xml:id="d797-f1"/> presently has total 9 armies in vicinity Nanfeng, in
                    eastern central Kiangsi Province. There are no reliable nor battle-tested
                    Nationalist troops to south of this concentration. Consequently, it appears that
                    Communists have capability take Canton within about 4 weeks, if not sooner.</p>
                <p>In order that we may make necessary plans for evacuation Embassy Office, would
                    appreciate you inform us if you can furnish LST or similar vessel stand by
                    Canton for movement Embassy Office personnel, files and effects to place of
                    safety should it become necessary.</p>
                <p>Repeated ComNavWesPac.<anchor n="45" xml:id="d797-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Clark</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d797-f1" n="44" xml:id="d797-f1-content">
                <p>Chinese Communist commander in Central China.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d797-f2" n="45" xml:id="d797-f2-content">
                <p>Commander, U.S. Naval Forces, Western Pacific, Vice Adm. Oscar C. Badger.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
